From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: hi846: Update the exposure limit on every format change

The exposure maximum follows height + vblank and is updated from the
V4L2_CID_VBLANK handler. set_fmt sets vblank to the new mode's default,
but the control framework calls s_ctrl only when the value changes: when
vblank already had that value (for instance 122 lines set in the
3264x2448 mode before switching to 1280x720, whose default is 122), the
exposure maximum stays at the old mode's 2448 + 122 - 2 lines instead of
840 until streaming starts and the control handler setup runs the
VBLANK handler again. Userspace that reads the limits after set_fmt, as
libcamera does when it configures, gets the old ones. Set the limit for
the new height in set_fmt as well.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/media/i2c/hi846.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/hi846.c b/drivers/media/i2c/hi846.c
index edd279563..704892eaa 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/hi846.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/hi846.c
@@ -1900,6 +1900,7 @@ static int hi846_set_format(struct v4l2_subdev *sd,
 	const struct hi846_datafmt *fmt = hi846_find_datafmt(mf->code);
 	u32 tgt_fps;
 	s32 vblank_def, h_blank;
+	s64 exposure_max;
 
 	if (!fmt) {
 		mf->code = hi846_colour_fmts[0].code;
@@ -1960,6 +1961,16 @@ static int hi846_set_format(struct v4l2_subdev *sd,
 				 HI846_FLL_MAX - hi846->cur_mode->height, 1,
 				 vblank_def);
 	__v4l2_ctrl_s_ctrl(hi846->vblank, vblank_def);
+	/*
+	 * The exposure limit follows height + vblank, but s_ctrl only runs when
+	 * vblank changes: keep the limit right for the new height when vblank
+	 * already had this value.
+	 */
+	exposure_max = hi846->cur_mode->height + hi846->vblank->val -
+		       HI846_EXPOSURE_MAX_MARGIN;
+	__v4l2_ctrl_modify_range(hi846->exposure, hi846->exposure->minimum,
+				 exposure_max, hi846->exposure->step,
+				 exposure_max);
 
 	h_blank = hi846->cur_mode->llp - hi846->cur_mode->width;
 
